            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The water-based sealants on our list, OSI SC-175, Titebond 2892, Green Glue, Auralex StopGap and Liquid Nails AS-825, are all listed as paintable once they have set or dried. Non-curing butyl acoustical sealants such as Tremco's are generally not meant to be painted and stay tacky, so keep those out of sight."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Green Glue sealant the same as Green Glue compound?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. The compound is a damping material applied between two sheets of drywall to turn them into a damped panel. The sealant is a caulk for the edges and penetrations of the wall. A Green Glue wall uses both: compound across the sheet and sealant at the perimeter, boxes and gaps."
          }
